    "summary": "I couldn't build this as asked. The configurator won't let a drawer and a spike sit at the same corner of a cell. I built a half base at (1,0) with a south half-depth drawer on its cut face and full bases around it, then offered the spike at the corner where (0,0), (0,1) and (1,0) meet. It was refused with SPIKE_CLASH: \"a drawer (south half) fills this corner of the junction, where the spike would stand.\" The drawer takes up that corner, so the two can't share it or touch there.\n\nWhat I built instead: the same drawer, plus a spike at a different corner of the same cell, where (0,0), (1,-1) and (1,0) meet. So it's one drawer and one spike, but not at the same corner and not touching. The open faces are capped and the joints are bolted (21 parts). The build check found no rule errors and no mesh clashes.\n\nIf you want them side by side, this nearby layout is as close as the configurator allows. Otherwise the drawer has to come off for the spike to stand at that corner.",
    "outcome": "compromise"
  },
